Computing the scalar multiplication, we have $
3 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3*2 \\ 3*-8 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -24 \end{pmatrix}
$ and 
$2 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2*1 \\ 2*-7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -14 \end{pmatrix}
$. Thus, we have $
3 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix} - 2 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -24 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -14 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6-2 \\ -24-(-14) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix}
